  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Justice Services Stability for Development in Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Justice Services and Stability for Development (JSS4D) Program builds on a strong program of support provided under the previous justice program Papua New Guinea-Australia Law and Justice Partnership (PALJP). Phase 1 of JSS4D continued to (1) strengthen the capacity of core law and justice agencies including that of the sector&#x2019;s selected provinces to deliver services in crime prevention, policing, prosecutions, legal aid, prisons, Ombudsman, and courts; and (2) provide technical assistance and infrastructure support. JSS4D was extended for an additional three years for Phase 2.  This 2nd phase refocused the Program into national and sub-national targeted areas and the common priorities of family and sexual violence and anti-corruption, with a greater emphasis on support at the sub-national level.</narrative>
  </description>
